#N CPU: a register machine factoring 15 (Carlini, Part 4)
#O Nicholas Carlini, 2021
#C His Part 4 computer, an unlimited register machine with 16 four-bit registers and a ROM of up to 128 instructions, running a program that searches for the factors of 15. It equals his animation cell for cell, and in this engine it follows its program through generation 245 million, about a quarter of the way: the whole program takes about 876 million generations.
#C Part 4: A Simple CPU on the Game of Life - Part 4 (2021-12-30)
#C https://nicholas.carlini.com/writing/2021/unlimited-register-machine-game-of-life.html
#C The unlimited register machine animated at the top of the post ("running a program that factors the number 15").
#C Recovered from frame 0 of the page's replay: /writing/2021/gameoflife/xdata2.js (xdata1.js holds the same first frame),
#C decoded with his own 2021 replay.js (decompress, unflattentrees, grid_undifference) in a sandbox, each 150-cell block
#C placed at its tile (every block of frame 0 unrotated). Frame k of the replay is generation 1025 k of this board.
#C Coordinates are the replay's: x = 150 * tile x + x in block, y = 150 * tile y + y in block.
#CXRLE Pos=153,154
